# Pins for the special-function operators.  incbeta's error check
# tested the pointer rather than *err, so icb returned 0 for interior
# x; observed by the differential operator fuzzer (tools/fuzz_eval.R)
# comparing every documented operator against R, and after the
# one-character change the two agree everywhere tested.  (Practical
# impact was likely small; the combination seems never to have been
# exercised.)  Conventions observed by the same fuzzer:
# mr = hazard rate dnorm/(1-pnorm) (reciprocal of the textbook Mill
# ratio); td(x,df) = pt(|x|,df), sign-blind; poisson(mean, count),
# integer count; icb(x,a,b) regularized = R pbeta(x,a,b).
nvar(dfile=one.dat, U[2.0]=c1,
  E1[24.12]=icb(0.5,2,2),
  E2[24.12]=icb(0.5,2,3),
  E3[24.12]=icb(0.25,1,1),
  E4[24.12]=td(1.5,10),
  E5[24.12]=td(0-1.5,10),
  E6[24.12]=mr(1.0),
  E7[24.12]=poisson(3,2),
  E8[24.12]=chd(2.5,4),
  E9[24.12]=icg(2.5,3),
);
pdata(keep=E1,E2,E3,E4,E5,E6,E7,E8,E9) = gf.out;
